The engines use only the standard library of their language. No third-party
code is included in this repository.

The packs under packs/ and the model modules under model/ were written from the
third-party sources below. The source files are not included. A pack records
field names, field numbers, positions, types, units and code values. Each
pack's PROVENANCE.md and the `source` lines of its pack.def state the exact
version, the SHA-256 of each file read and the license statement of the source.
The license of each source is given here as that source states it.

Pack a-gra; module agra
  Autonomy Government Reference Architecture (A-GRA) schema 6.0a (version
  006.0.ASK), U.S. Air Force. https://github.com/open-arsenal/a-gra
  File header: Distribution Statement A. Approved for public release:
  distribution is unlimited.

Pack uci; module uci
  Universal Command and Control Interface (UCI) schema 2.6 (version 002.6.0),
  U.S. Air Force. https://github.com/open-arsenal/uci
  File header: Distribution Statement A. Approved for public release:
  distribution is unlimited.

Packs isa, isa-message, isa-ipl1, isa-xml; modules isa, isa1, isaxml
  Integrated Sensor Architecture (ISA) schema set 6.0.13: IPL 3.7 and IPL 1.6
  protobuf declaration files, IPL 4.7 XML schema.
  File header: Distribution Statement A. Approved for Public Release.
  Distribution is Unlimited. The files carry no license text and no copyright
  line.

Packs sapient, sapient-v1; modules sapient, sapient1
  SAPIENT protobuf files, BSI Flex 335 v2.0 and v1.0, Defence Science and
  Technology Laboratory (Dstl). https://github.com/dstl/SAPIENT-Proto-Files
  Crown owned Copyright 2023. Apache License, Version 2.0.

Pack cot-protobuf; module takproto
  TAK protocol version 1 protobuf definitions, from
  https://github.com/deptofdefense/AndroidTacticalAssaultKit-CIV (directory
  takproto). The repository's LICENSE.md is the GNU General Public License,
  Version 3; its INTENT.md states that portions written by U.S. Federal
  government employees are ineligible for copyright protection in the U.S.
  The .proto files carry no license or copyright header. Field numbers, names
  and types only.

Pack cot-xml; module core
  Cursor on Target event schema, The MITRE Corporation, approved for public
  release.

Pack canonical-track-v2; module track
  Canonical Track v2 schema, https://github.com/USAREUR-AF/open-billie
  Apache License, Version 2.0.

Pack nmea2000; module n2k
  CANboat database (docs/canboat.json), version 9.2.0.
  https://github.com/canboat/canboat
  (C) 2009-2026, Kees Verruijt, Harlingen, The Netherlands. Apache License,
  Version 2.0.

Pack mavlink2; module mavlink
  MAVLink message definitions (common.xml, standard.xml, minimal.xml).
  https://github.com/mavlink/mavlink
  The repository's COPYING file states the GNU Lesser General Public License,
  version 3, with an exception that places generated code under the MIT
  license. The XML files carry no license header. Message names and ids, field
  names, types, array lengths, units and enumeration values only; no
  description text.

Pack remote-id; module rid
  opendroneid-core-c, the reference implementation of ASTM F3411 message
  contents. https://github.com/opendroneid/opendroneid-core-c
  Copyright (C) 2019 Intel Corporation. Apache License, Version 2.0.

Pack adsb; module adsb
  Junzi Sun, "The 1090 Megahertz Riddle: A Guide to Decoding Mode S and ADS-B
  Signals", second edition, TU Delft OPEN Publishing.
  https://mode-s.org/1090mhz/  Copyright 2021 Junzi Sun. CC BY-NC-SA 4.0.
  Field positions, widths, code meanings and five example messages; no text,
  table or figure.
  pyModeS, https://github.com/junzis/pyModeS  GNU General Public License,
  Version 3. Published test messages and their decoded values; no code.

Pack geojson
  IETF RFC 7946, The GeoJSON Format.

Pack nvg
  NATO Vector Graphics 1.5 XML schema, NATO Allied Command Transformation.

The packs named conformance*, demo-* and the module probe describe synthetic
formats written for this project and have no external source.
